# PREAMBLE

Sovereign Shards is a sovereign computing ecosystem conceived, designed, and originated by Mike McCollum.

The purpose of Sovereign Shards is to enable individuals, creators, developers, communities, organizations, agents, and future generations of participants to build, own, and operate digital worlds, software systems, knowledge systems, businesses, creative works, and sovereign technological infrastructure.

This License exists to establish a covenant between the Platform and its participants.

The intent of this covenant is simple:

* Creators should own what they create.
* Contributors should receive recognition for what they contribute.
* Developers should be free to build.
* Businesses should be free to operate.
* Innovation should be encouraged.
* Stewardship should be preserved.
* The Sovereign Shards platform should remain protected.
* The Sovereign Shards ecosystem should not be appropriated, rebranded, fragmented, or commercialized by parties seeking to claim ownership of the platform itself.

Sovereign Shards is not a public-domain project.

Sovereign Shards is not an abandoned commons.

Sovereign Shards is not a platform intended to be forked into competing ecosystems.

Sovereign Shards is a living ecosystem under active stewardship.

This License grants broad rights to participate in the ecosystem while reserving ownership of the platform itself.

---

# ARTICLE I — DEFINITIONS

For purposes of this License:

"Platform" means Sovereign Shards and all official software, services, infrastructure, repositories, protocols, documentation, systems, and distributions designated as part of the Sovereign Shards ecosystem.

"Platform Owner" means Mike McCollum and any successor entity designated by Mike McCollum to steward Sovereign Shards.

"Core Technology" means any runtime, execution engine, kernel, orchestration system, platform infrastructure, protocol, framework, platform service, marketplace service, identity service, or foundational technology designated as part of the Sovereign Shards core.

"Ecosystem Components" means APIs, SDKs, templates, examples, plugin systems, integration layers, development tooling, documentation examples, and public developer resources.

"Creator Works" means any shard, world, plugin, application, workflow, service, dataset, prompt collection, story, artwork, business, content, or derivative creation produced by a participant using the Platform.

"Contributor" means any individual or organization contributing code, documentation, designs, assets, ideas, fixes, improvements, or other materials to the Platform.

"Official Distribution" means any distribution approved by the Platform Owner.

---

# ARTICLE II — PRINCIPLE OF SOVEREIGNTY

The central principle of Sovereign Shards is sovereignty.

The Platform exists to empower participants rather than extract ownership from them.

Accordingly:

You own what you create.

You retain ownership of your works.

You retain ownership of your businesses.

You retain ownership of your ideas.

You retain ownership of your worlds, shards, plugins, services, assets, workflows, stories, and intellectual property.

The Platform does not claim ownership of Creator Works solely because they were created using Sovereign Shards.

At the same time:

The Platform remains the property of its owner.

Participation does not transfer ownership.

Contribution does not transfer ownership.

Use does not transfer ownership.

Extension does not transfer ownership.

The right to build upon the Platform is not the right to take the Platform itself.

---

# ARTICLE III — PLATFORM OWNERSHIP

All rights not expressly granted under this License remain reserved.

Ownership of the Platform includes but is not limited to:

* Core architecture
* Runtime systems
* Platform infrastructure
* Execution engines
* Kernel systems
* Orchestration systems
* Official repositories
* Official documentation
* Official distributions
* Official marketplaces
* Official hosted services
* Official governance structures
* Official branding

Nothing within this License transfers ownership of the Platform to any user, contributor, developer, organization, or third party.

---

# ARTICLE IV — CREATOR RIGHTS

Creators retain full ownership of Creator Works.

Creator Works include but are not limited to:

* Shards
* Worlds
* Plugins
* Applications
* Services
* Businesses
* Workflows
* Datasets
* Characters
* Stories
* Artwork
* Content
* Assets
* Intellectual property

Creators may:

* Publish Creator Works
* License Creator Works
* Sell Creator Works
* Open-source Creator Works
* Commercialize Creator Works
* Transfer Creator Works
* Build businesses from Creator Works

The Platform Owner does not claim ownership of Creator Works solely because they were created using the Platform.

---

# ARTICLE V — PERMITTED USE

Participants may:

* Use the Platform
* Learn from the Platform
* Build upon the Platform
* Extend the Platform through approved mechanisms
* Create plugins
* Create integrations
* Create applications
* Create businesses
* Create educational materials
* Operate commercial services based on Creator Works

Commercial activity based on Creator Works is expressly permitted.

The success of creators is considered beneficial to the ecosystem.

---

# ARTICLE VI — CONTRIBUTIONS

Contributors retain authorship of their contributions.

By contributing to official Sovereign Shards repositories, Contributors grant the Platform Owner a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free license to:

* Use contributions
* Modify contributions
* Incorporate contributions
* Redistribute contributions
* Commercialize contributions as part of the Platform
* Maintain contributions
* Archive contributions

Contributors represent that they possess sufficient rights to submit their contributions.

Contributors may continue using their own contributions elsewhere unless restricted by separate agreements.

---

# ARTICLE VII — PROTECTION OF THE PLATFORM

Without explicit written permission from the Platform Owner, no person or organization may:

* Fork the Platform and distribute it as a competing platform
* Fork the Platform and rebrand it
* Remove authorship notices
* Remove copyright notices
* Remove licensing notices
* Present the Platform as their own creation
* Offer the Platform itself as a competing hosted service
* Redistribute modified Core Technology
* Create derivative platforms substantially based on Core Technology for purposes of competing with Sovereign Shards
* Misrepresent affiliation with Sovereign Shards

The Platform may be extended.

The Platform may not be appropriated.

---

# ARTICLE VIII — COMMERCIAL RIGHTS

Commercial use of Creator Works is permitted.

Commercial use of plugins is permitted.

Commercial use of applications built on the Platform is permitted.

Commercial operation of businesses built on the Platform is permitted.

Commercial redistribution of Core Technology is prohibited without authorization.

Enterprise, OEM, white-label, embedded, and redistribution rights may be granted separately by the Platform Owner.

---

# ARTICLE IX — THIRD-PARTY OWNERSHIP

Not all entities associated with the ecosystem are owned by the Platform Owner.

Contributors retain ownership of their independent intellectual property.

Creators retain ownership of their Creator Works.

Organizations retain ownership of their own brands and assets.

Agents, contributors, projects, communities, brands, characters, systems, and associated works remain the property of their respective owners unless ownership is explicitly transferred in writing.

Participation in the ecosystem does not transfer ownership.

Association does not imply ownership.

---

# ARTICLE X — BRANDING

The names, marks, symbols, visual identities, logos, and branding associated with Sovereign Shards are protected and reserved.

Derivative projects may not represent themselves as official Sovereign Shards projects.

Forks, derivatives, or independent projects must clearly identify themselves as independent.

Use of Sovereign Shards branding does not imply endorsement.

No rights to Platform branding are granted except where expressly authorized.

---

# ARTICLE XI — COMMUNITY COVENANT

The Platform exists to empower creators.

The ecosystem seeks to support:

* Ownership
* Creativity
* Innovation
* Sovereignty
* Collaboration
* Knowledge sharing
* Long-term stewardship

The Platform is not intended to extract ownership from creators.

The Platform seeks alignment between creator success and platform success.

Participants are encouraged to build boldly, contribute responsibly, and respect the sovereignty of others.

---

# ARTICLE XII — PLATFORM STEWARDSHIP

The Platform Owner serves as steward of Sovereign Shards.

The purpose of stewardship is preservation of identity, continuity, direction, and integrity.

The ecosystem may grow beyond its creator.

The ecosystem may evolve.

The ecosystem may transform.

Its origin shall nevertheless remain acknowledged.

The Sovereign Shards architecture, ecosystem concept, and platform vision originated with Mike McCollum.

Recognition of contribution does not erase origin.

Recognition of origin does not diminish contribution.

Both shall be preserved.

---

