# ARTICLE XIV — LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE PLATFORM OWNER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, PUNITIVE, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OF THE PLATFORM.

THIS LIMITATION APPLIES REGARDLESS OF THE THEORY OF LIABILITY.

---

# ARTICLE XV — TERMINATION

Rights granted under this License terminate automatically upon material violation of its terms.

Upon termination:

* Access rights may be revoked.
* Distribution rights cease.
* Commercial rights cease.
* Platform rights cease.

Ownership provisions, attribution provisions, disclaimers, and liability limitations survive termination.

---

# ARTICLE XVI — GUIDING PRINCIPLE

The Platform belongs to its steward.

The creations belong to their creators.

You own what you create.

You may build.

You may innovate.

You may prosper.

You may contribute.

You may create worlds that exceed anything imagined by the Platform Owner.

You may not take the Platform itself, rename it, and present it as your own.

That distinction preserves both creator sovereignty and platform continuity.

